      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef maximum_time(time: str) -> str:\n    # Split the time into hours and minutes\n    hours, minutes = time.split(\":\")\n\n    # Replace '?' in hours part\n    if hours[0] == '?':\n        # If the second digit of hour is not '?' and less than 4, we can safely set the first digit to '1'\n        # because '1?' can't be '20', '21', ..., '23', which are all invalid hours for 12-hour format.\n        hours = ('1' if minutes[0] != '?' and int(minutes[0]) < 4 else '2') + hours[1]\n    if hours[1] == '?':\n        # If the first digit of hour is '2', the second digit can only be '3', '4', '5', or '9'\n        # to make the hour valid ('23', '24', '25', '29').\n        hours = hours[0] + ('9' if hours[0] == '2' else '9')\n\n    # Replace '?' in minutes part\n    if minutes[0] == '?':\n        minutes = '5' + minutes[1]  # Set the first minute digit to '5' to make it as large as possible\n    if minutes[1] == '?':\n        minutes = minutes[0] + '9'  # Set the second minute digit to '9' for maximum minutes\n\n    # Combine hours and minutes back to the final time string\n    return hours + \":\" + minutes\n```",
