    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Below is the Python function body that implements the game rules described in the prompt and returns the list of losers:\n\n```python\ndef find_game_losers(n, k):\n    # Initialize an array to track if a friend has received the ball\n    has_received_ball = [False] * (n + 1)\n    current_friend = 1\n    steps = k\n    \n    # Continue the game until a friend receives the ball for the second time\n    while True:\n        next_friend = (current_friend + steps - 1) % n + 1\n        if has_received_ball[next_friend]:\n            break\n        has_received_ball[next_friend] = True\n        current_friend = next_friend\n        steps += k\n\n    # Identify all friends who have not received the ball\n    losers = [i for i in range(1, n + 1) if not has_received_ball[i]]\n    \n    return losers\n```\n\nThis function maintains a list to keep track of whether each friend has received the ball. The game continues until a friend receives the ball a second time. After the game ends, the function creates a list of the friends who have not received the ball and returns it.",
