      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef can_create_ideal_sheet():\n    import sys\n    input = sys.stdin.read\n    data = input().split()\n    \n    # Read dimensions and content of sheet A\n    H_A, W_A = int(data[0]), int(data[1])\n    A = data[2:H_A+2]\n    \n    # Read dimensions and content of sheet B\n    H_B, W_B = int(data[H_A+2]), int(data[H_A+3])\n    B = data[H_A+4:H_A+4+H_B]\n    \n    # Read dimensions and content of ideal sheet X\n    H_X, W_X = int(data[H_A+4+H_B]), int(data[H_A+4+H_B+1])\n    X = data[H_A+4+H_B+2:H_A+4+H_B+2+H_X]\n    \n    # Convert sheets to boolean matrices (True for black, False for transparent)\n    A = [[c == '#' for c in row] for row in A]\n    B = [[c == '#' for c in row] for row in B]\n    X = [[c == '#' for c in row] for row in X]\n    \n    # Function to check if sheet X can be formed by pasting A and B\n    def can_form_X():\n        # Try all possible top-left corners for the cut-out area\n        for start_i in range(-H_A + 1, H_B):\n            for start_j in range(-W_A + 1, W_B):\n                # Check if this position can cover all black squares of A and B\n                if all((start_i + i < 0 or start_i + i >= H_X or\n                        start_j + j < 0 or start_j + j >= W_X or\n                        not (A[i][j] or B[i][start_i + i - start_j][j])) for i in range(H_A) for j in range(W_A)):\n                    continue\n                if all((start_i + i < 0 or start_i + i >= H_X or\n                        start_j + j < 0 or start_j + j >= W_X or\n                        not (A[i][j] or B[i][start_i + i - start_j][j])) for i in range(H_B) for j in range(W_B)):\n                    continue\n                # Check if the cut-out area matches X\n                if all((start_i + i >= 0 and start_i + i < H_X and\n                        start_j + j >= 0 and start_j + j < W_X and\n                        X[i][j] == (A[i][j] or B[i][start_i + i - start_j][j])) for i in range(H_X) for j in range(W_X)):\n                    return True\n        return False\n    \n    # Output the result\n    if can_form_X():\n        print('Yes')\n    else:\n        print('No')\n\n# Call the function to execute\ncan_create_ideal_sheet()\n```",
