      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef can_fill_grid():\n    # Read the input and construct the grid\n    grid = [input() for _ in range(12)]\n    \n    # Function to rotate a polyomino 90 degrees clockwise\n    def rotate(p):\n        return [''.join([p[3-i][j] for i in range(4)]) for j in range(4)]\n    \n    # Function to check if a polyomino can fit in the grid at a given position\n    def can_place(grid, polyomino, x, y):\n        for i in range(4):\n            for j in range(4):\n                if polyomino[i][j] == '#' and grid[x + i][y + j] != '.':\n                    return False\n        return True\n    \n    # Function to place a polyomino in the grid\n    def place(grid, polyomino, x, y):\n        for i in range(4):\n            for j in range(4):\n                if polyomino[i][j] == '#':\n                    grid[x + i][y + j] = '#'\n    \n    # Function to remove a polyomino from the grid\n    def remove(grid, polyomino, x, y):\n        for i in range(4):\n            for j in range(4):\n                if polyomino[i][j] == '#':\n                    grid[x + i][y + j] = '.'\n    \n    # Function to try to fit all polyominoes in the grid\n    def fit_polyominoes(grid, index=0):\n        if index == len(polyominos):\n            return True\n        for x in range(8 - len(polyominos[index])):\n            for y in range(8 - len(polyominos[index][0])):\n                if can_place(grid, polyominos[index], x, y):\n                    place(grid, polyominos[index], x, y)\n                    if fit_polyominoes(grid, index + 1):\n                        return True\n                    remove(grid, polyominos[index], x, y)\n        return False\n    \n    # Split the input into three polyominoes and rotate them\n    polyominos = [list(input().strip()) for _ in range(4)]\n    polyominos += [list(input().strip()) for _ in range(4)]\n    polyominos += [list(input().strip()) for _ in range(4)]\n    \n    # Generate all rotations for each polyomino\n    rotations = []\n    for p in polyominos:\n        for _ in range(4):\n            p = rotate(p)\n            rotations.append(p)\n    \n    # Check all combinations of placing the polyominos\n    for i in range(len(rotations)):\n        for j in range(i + 1, len(rotations)):\n            for k in range(j + 1, len(rotations)):\n                # Create a copy of the grid for each combination\n                grid_copy = [row[:] for row in grid]\n                if fit_polyominoes(grid_copy, 0):\n                    print('Yes')\n                    return\n    \n    print('No')\n\n# Call the function to execute\ncan_fill_grid()\n```",
