      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    # Read integers V1, V2, V3 from standard input\n    V1, V2, V3 = map(int, input().split())\n\n    # Check if the provided V1, V2, V3 can form a valid configuration\n    if V1 % 49 != 0 or V2 % 7 != 0 or V3 % 1 != 0:\n        print('No')\n        return\n    \n    # Calculate the number of unit cubes in each category\n    num_single_cubes = V1 // 49\n    num_double_cubes = V2 // 7\n    num_triple_cubes = V3\n    \n    # Calculate the total number of unit cubes that need to be covered\n    total_cubes = 3 * 7 * 7 * 7\n    remaining_cubes = total_cubes - num_single_cubes * 7 - num_double_cubes * 2 - num_triple_cubes\n    \n    # Check if the remaining number of cubes can be arranged in a valid way\n    if remaining_cubes < 0 or (remaining_cubes % 2 != 0 and remaining_cubes != 0):\n        print('No')\n        return\n    \n    # Calculate the number of pairs of unit cubes that need to be placed in the same position\n    num_pairs = remaining_cubes // 2 if remaining_cubes != 0 else 0\n    \n    # Initialize the positions of the cubes\n    positions = [(0, 0, 0)] * (num_single_cubes + num_double_cubes + num_triple_cubes + num_pairs)\n    \n    # Fill positions for single covered cubes\n    for i in range(num_single_cubes):\n        positions[i] = (0, 0, i * 2)\n    \n    # Fill positions for double covered cubes\n    for i in range(num_double_cubes):\n        positions[num_single_cubes + i] = (0, i * 2, 0)\n    \n    # Fill positions for triple covered cubes\n    for i in range(num_triple_cubes):\n        positions[num_single_cubes + num_double_cubes + i] = (i * 2, 0, 0)\n    \n    # Fill positions for pairs of cubes\n    for i in range(num_pairs):\n        positions[num_single_cubes + num_double_cubes + num_triple_cubes + i] = (i * 2, i * 2, i * 2)\n    \n    # Adjust positions to ensure all coordinates are within the valid range\n    for i in range(len(positions)):\n        x, y, z = positions[i]\n        positions[i] = (x - 7 * (x // 7), y - 7 * (y // 7), z - 7 * (z // 7))\n    \n    # Output the result\n    print('Yes')\n    print(' '.join(str(pos) for pos in positions))\n\n# Call the solve function to execute\nsolve()\n```",
