      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\ninput = sys.stdin.read\n\ndef solve():\n    data = input().split()\n    H = int(data[0])\n    W = int(data[1])\n    S = [data[i + 2] for i in range(H)]\n\n    MOD = 998244353\n\n    # Helper function to find connected components using DFS\n    def dfs(x, y, visited, grid):\n        stack = [(x, y)]\n        component_size = 0\n        while stack:\n            cx, cy = stack.pop()\n            if visited[cx][cy]:\n                continue\n            visited[cx][cy] = True\n            component_size += 1\n            for dx, dy in [(-1, 0), (1, 0), (0, -1), (0, 1)]:\n                nx, ny = cx + dx, cy + dy\n                if 0 <= nx < H and 0 <= ny < W and not visited[nx][ny] and grid[nx][ny] == '#':\n                    stack.append((nx, ny))\n        return component_size\n\n    # Count initial green components\n    visited = [[False] * W for _ in range(H)]\n    initial_components = 0\n    for i in range(H):\n        for j in range(W):\n            if S[i][j] == '#' and not visited[i][j]:\n                initial_components += 1\n                dfs(i, j, visited, S)\n\n    # Count the number of green cells and calculate the expected value\n    green_cells = sum(S[i][j] == '#' for i in range(H) for j in range(W))\n    total_cells = H * W\n    expected_value = (initial_components * total_cells + green_cells) * pow(total_cells - 1, MOD - 2, MOD)\n    print(expected_value % MOD)\n\n# Call the function to execute\nsolve()\n```",
