    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To solve the problem, we can create a Python function that calculates the sum of the power of all possible non-empty groups of heroes. The main challenge is to efficiently calculate the contribution of each element to the sum without explicitly generating all possible groups, as the number of such groups grows exponentially with the length of the input array.\n\nHere is the Python function that calculates the desired sum:\n\n```python\ndef sum_of_powers(nums):\n    MOD = 10**9 + 7\n    n = len(nums)\n    nums.sort()\n    total_sum = 0\n    \n    # Precompute powers of 2 up to n for counting combinations\n    power_of_two = [1] * (n + 1)\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        power_of_two[i] = (power_of_two[i - 1] * 2) % MOD\n\n    # Calculate prefix and suffix sums for max and min calculations\n    prefix_min = [0] * n\n    prefix_max = [0] * n\n    suffix_min = [0] * n\n    suffix_max = [0] * n\n\n    # Fill prefix min and max arrays\n    prefix_min[0] = nums[0]\n    prefix_max[0] = nums[0]\n    for i in range(1, n):\n        prefix_min[i] = min(prefix_min[i-1], nums[i])\n        prefix_max[i] = max(prefix_max[i-1], nums[i])\n\n    # Fill suffix min and max arrays\n    suffix_min[n-1] = nums[n-1]\n    suffix_max[n-1] = nums[n-1]\n    for i in range(n-2, -1, -1):\n        suffix_min[i] = min(suffix_min[i+1], nums[i])\n        suffix_max[i] = max(suffix_max[i+1], nums[i])\n\n    # Calculate the contribution of each element being the min and max in a group\n    for i in range(n):\n        if i > 0 and nums[i] == prefix_min[i-1]:\n            max_contrib = (prefix_max[i-1] ** 2 * power_of_two[i]) % MOD\n        else:\n            max_contrib = (nums[i] ** 2 * power_of_two[i]) % MOD\n\n        if i < n-1 and nums[i] == suffix_min[i+1]:\n            min_contrib = (suffix_max[i+1] ** 2 * power_of_two[n-i-1]) % MOD\n        else:\n            min_contrib = (nums[i] ** 2 * power_of_two[n-i-1]) % MOD\n\n        total_sum = (total_sum + max_contrib + min_contrib) % MOD\n\n    return total_sum\n```\n\nThis function first sorts the array and precomputes powers of two modulo \\(10^9 + 7\\) for later combination calculations. It then computes prefix and suffix arrays for both minimum and maximum values. After that, it iterates over the array to calculate the contribution of each element being the minimum or maximum in a group, taking into account the number of possible groups that can be formed with that element as the minimum or maximum. The final sum is computed modulo \\(10^9 + 7\\). This approach avoids generating all groups explicitly and computes the result in \\(O(n)\\) time.",
