    "prediction": "glm-4-air",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Here's a Python function that counts the number of right triangles in a 2D boolean matrix according to the provided prompt:\n\n```python\ndef count_right_triangles(grid):\n    def is_valid_triangle(x1, y1, x2, y2, x3, y3):\n        # Check if the points form a right triangle\n        return grid[x1][y1] == 1 and grid[x2][y2] == 1 and grid[x3][y3] == 1\n\n    rows = len(grid)\n    cols = len(grid[0]) if rows > 0 else 0\n    triangle_count = 0\n\n    # Iterate through all cells to find potential right triangles\n    for i in range(rows):\n        for j in range(cols):\n            if grid[i][j] == 1:  # grid[i][j] is a potential top vertex of the triangle\n                # Check for right triangle in all four possible configurations\n                for k in range(j + 1, cols):  # Potential right vertex along the row\n                    if grid[i][k] == 1:\n                        # Check for potential bottom vertex in the column\n                        for l in range(i + 1, rows):\n                            if grid[l][k] == 1:\n                                # We found a right triangle (i, j), (i, k), (l, k)\n                                triangle_count += 1\n                for k in range(i + 1, rows):  # Potential right vertex along the column\n                    if grid[k][j] == 1:\n                        # Check for potential bottom vertex in the row\n                        for l in range(j + 1, cols):\n                            if grid[k][l] == 1:\n                                # We found a right triangle (i, j), (k, j), (k, l)\n                                triangle_count += 1\n\n    return triangle_count\n``` \n\nThis function iterates over the matrix and checks all combinations of three points that could potentially form a right triangle. When it finds a set of three points that all have the value 1 and satisfy the right triangle condition (one point in the same row as another and in the same column as the third), it increments the triangle count.",
