      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef can_reach_goal():\n    import sys\n    input = sys.stdin.read\n    data = input().split()\n    \n    # Read grid dimensions\n    H = int(data[0])\n    W = int(data[1])\n    \n    # Initialize the grid and variables to track start and goal positions\n    grid = []\n    start_y = start_x = goal_y = goal_x = -1\n    \n    index = 2\n    for y in range(H):\n        row = data[index + y]\n        grid.append(row)\n        if 'S' in row:\n            start_y, start_x = y, row.index('S')\n        if 'T' in row:\n            goal_y, goal_x = y, row.index('T')\n    \n    # Read number of medicines\n    N = int(data[index + H])\n    index += H + 1\n    \n    # Store medicines information\n    medicines = []\n    for _ in range(N):\n        r = int(data[index]) - 1\n        c = int(data[index + 1]) - 1\n        e = int(data[index + 2])\n        medicines.append((r, c, e))\n        index += 3\n    \n    # BFS setup\n    from collections import deque\n    queue = deque([(start_y, start_x, 0)])\n    visited = [[False] * W for _ in range(H)]\n    visited[start_y][start_x] = True\n    \n    # BFS to find if the goal is reachable\n    directions = [(1, 0), (-1, 0), (0, 1), (0, -1)]\n    while queue:\n        y, x, energy = queue.popleft()\n        \n        # Check if we reached the goal\n        if (y, x) == (goal_y, goal_x):\n            print(\"Yes\")\n            return\n        \n        # Process the current cell\n        for dy, dx in directions:\n            ny, nx = y + dy, x + dx\n            if 0 <= ny < H and 0 <= nx < W and grid[ny][nx] != '#':\n                # Calculate new energy after moving\n                new_energy = energy - 1\n                \n                # Check if there's a medicine in the new cell\n                for r, c, e in medicines:\n                    if r == ny and c == nx:\n                        new_energy = e\n                        break\n                \n                # Continue only if energy is positive and cell is not visited\n                if new_energy > 0 and not visited[ny][nx]:\n                    visited[ny][nx] = True\n                    queue.append((ny, nx, new_energy))\n    \n    # If goal was not reached\n    print(\"No\")\n\n# Call the function to execute\ncan_reach_goal()\n```",
