      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef simulate_takahashi():\n    import sys\n    input = sys.stdin.read\n    data = input().strip()\n    H, W, N = map(int, data.split())\n\n    # Initialize the grid\n    grid = [['.'] * W for _ in range(H)]\n\n    # Directions correspond to [up, right, down, left]\n    directions = [(1, 0), (0, 1), (-1, 0), (0, -1)]\n    current_direction = 0  # start facing up\n    current_row, current_col = 0, 0\n\n    for _ in range(N):\n        if grid[current_row][current_col] == '.':\n            # Paint black and rotate clockwise\n            grid[current_row][current_col] = '#'\n            current_direction = (current_direction + 1) % 4\n        else:\n            # Paint white and rotate counterclockwise\n            grid[current_row][current_col] = '.'\n            current_direction = (current_direction - 1) % 4\n        \n        # Move forward in the current direction\n        dr, dc = directions[current_direction]\n        current_row = (current_row + dr) % H\n        current_col = (current_col + dc) % W\n\n    # Print the grid\n    for row in grid:\n        print(''.join(row))\n\n# Call the function to execute\nsimulate_takahashi()\n```",
