      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef calculate_probability():\n    # Reading the 3x3 grid from standard input\n    c = [list(map(int, input().split())) for _ in range(3)]\n    \n    # Calculate the total number of permutations of the grid\n    total_permutations = 1\n    for i in range(3):\n        for j in range(3):\n            total_permutations *= 9 - i * 3 - j\n    \n    # Calculate the number of favorable outcomes\n    favorable_outcomes = 0\n    for i in range(3):\n        for j in range(3):\n            # Count the number of permutations starting with c[i][j]\n            permutations_starting_with_cij = 1\n            for x in range(3):\n                for y in range(3):\n                    if x == i or y == j or (x + y == i + j) or (x - y == i - j):\n                        continue\n                    permutations_starting_with_cij *= 9 - x * 3 - y - (1 if c[x][y] == c[i][j] else 0)\n            \n            # Add the number of favorable outcomes from this starting position\n            favorable_outcomes += permutations_starting_with_cij\n    \n    # Calculate the probability\n    probability = favorable_outcomes / total_permutations\n    \n    # Print the result with high precision\n    print(f\"{probability:.20f}\")\n\n# Call the function to execute\ncalculate_probability()\n```",
