    "prediction": "glm-4-air",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Here is the Python function body that solves the given problem:\n\n```python\ndef length_of_substring(s):\n    char_count = {}\n    max_length = 0\n    left = 0\n\n    for right in range(len(s)):\n        char = s[right]\n        char_count[char] = char_count.get(char, 0) + 1\n\n        while len(char_count) > 2 or (len(char_count) == 2 and char_count[char] > 2):\n            left_char = s[left]\n            char_count[left_char] -= 1\n            if char_count[left_char] == 0:\n                del char_count[left_char]\n            left += 1\n        \n        max_length = max(max_length, right - left + 1)\n    \n    return max_length\n```\n\nThis function uses a sliding window approach with two pointers, `left` and `right`, to keep track of the current substring. The `char_count` dictionary keeps track of the occurrences of each character within the window. The function iterates through the string, expanding the window by moving the `right` pointer, and shrinks the window by moving the `left` pointer when the condition of having at most two occurrences of each character is violated. The maximum length of the valid substring is updated accordingly.",
