      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef longest_special_substring(s):\n    max_length = -1\n    # Iterate through each character in the string to consider it as a potential special substring\n    for i in range(len(s)):\n        # Check for the current character repeating consecutively\n        current_char = s[i]\n        count = 0\n        while i + count < len(s) and s[i + count] == current_char:\n            count += 1\n        \n        # If the current character repeats at least 3 times, check if it's the longest found so far\n        if count >= 3:\n            max_length = max(max_length, count)\n        \n        # Move the index to the end of the current sequence of identical characters\n        i += count - 1\n\n    return max_length\n```",
