      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef identify_spilled_bottle():\n    import sys\n    input = sys.stdin.read\n    N = int(input().strip())\n    \n    # Determine the number of friends (minimum number of tests needed)\n    M = N.bit_length()  # This is the minimum number of friends needed to identify the spoiled bottle using binary representation\n    \n    # Output the number of friends\n    print(M)\n    \n    # Distribute the bottles among friends using binary representation\n    # Each friend will get bottles where the binary representation has a '1' in their position\n    for i in range(M):\n        # Calculate the bottles for each friend\n        bottles = [j + 1 for j in range(N) if (j >> i) & 1]\n        # Output the number of bottles and the bottles themselves\n        print(len(bottles), *bottles)\n    \n    # Read the results from the judge\n    results = input().strip()\n    \n    # Determine which bottle is spoiled based on the results\n    spoiled_index = 0\n    for i, result in enumerate(results):\n        if result == '1':\n            spoiled_index += 2**i\n    \n    # Output the spoiled bottle's number (1-indexed)\n    print(spoiled_index + 1)\n\n# Call the function to start the interactive process\nidentify_spilled_bottle()\n```",
