    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef count_boundary_returns(nums):\n    # Initialize the position of the ant to be 0 (on the boundary)\n    position = 0\n    # Initialize a counter to keep track of how many times the ant returns to the boundary\n    boundary_returns = 0\n\n    # Iterate over each number in the array\n    for num in nums:\n        # If the number is positive, the ant moves to the right\n        if num > 0:\n            # Check if the ant crosses the boundary during the movement\n            if position == -num:\n                boundary_returns += 1\n            position += num\n        # If the number is negative, the ant moves to the left\n        elif num < 0:\n            # Check if the ant crosses the boundary during the movement\n            if position == -num:\n                boundary_returns += 1\n            position += num\n\n    # Return the number of times the ant returned to the boundary\n    return boundary_returns\n```",
