    "prompt": "Generate an executable Python function generated from the given prompt. Return the function body without invoking it at the final solution. Question:\nYou are given an array arr of size n consisting of non-empty strings.\nFind a string array answer of size n such that:\n\nanswer[i] is the shortest substring of arr[i] that does not occur as a substring in any other string in arr. If multiple such substrings exist, answer[i] should be the lexicographically smallest. And if no such substring exists, answer[i] should be an empty string.\n\nReturn the array answer.\n \nExample 1:\n\nInput: arr = [\"cab\",\"ad\",\"bad\",\"c\"]\nOutput: [\"ab\",\"\",\"ba\",\"\"]\nExplanation: We have the following:\n- For the string \"cab\", the shortest substring that does not occur in any other string is either \"ca\" or \"ab\", we choose the lexicographically smaller substring, which is \"ab\".\n- For the string \"ad\", there is no substring that does not occur in any other string.\n- For the string \"bad\", the shortest substring that does not occur in any other string is \"ba\".\n- For the string \"c\", there is no substring that does not occur in any other string.\n\nExample 2:\n\nInput: arr = [\"abc\",\"bcd\",\"abcd\"]\nOutput: [\"\",\"\",\"abcd\"]\nExplanation: We have the following:\n- For the string \"abc\", there is no substring that does not occur in any other string.\n- For the string \"bcd\", there is no substring that does not occur in any other string.\n- For the string \"abcd\", the shortest substring that does not occur in any other string is \"abcd\".\n\n \nConstraints:\n\nn == arr.length\n2 <= n <= 100\n1 <= arr[i].length <= 20\narr[i] consists only of lowercase English letters.",
    "prediction": "glm-4-air",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Here's the Python function body that satisfies the prompt:\n\n```python\ndef shortest_unique_substrings(arr):\n    # Initialize an empty list to store the result\n    answer = []\n\n    # Create a dictionary to store all substrings of each string in arr\n    substrings_dict = {}\n\n    # Populate the dictionary with all possible substrings for each string\n    for s in arr:\n        substrings_dict[s] = set()\n        length = len(s)\n        for i in range(length):\n            for j in range(i + 1, length + 1):\n                substrings_dict[s].add(s[i:j])\n\n    # For each string in arr, find the shortest unique substring\n    for s in arr:\n        unique_substrings = set()\n        for sub in substrings_dict[s]:\n            is_unique = True\n            for other_s in arr:\n                if other_s != s and sub in substrings_dict[other_s]:\n                    is_unique = False\n                    break\n            if is_unique:\n                unique_substrings.add(sub)\n\n        # Find the shortest unique substring, if any\n        if unique_substrings:\n            shortest_unique = min(unique_substrings, key=lambda x: (len(x), x))\n            answer.append(shortest_unique)\n        else:\n            answer.append(\"\")\n\n    return answer\n``` \n\nThis function loops through each string in the input array `arr`, generates all possible substrings for each string, and checks if any of these substrings are unique (not present in any other string in `arr`). If a unique substring is found, it is added to the `unique_substrings` set for that string. Finally, the function determines the shortest unique substring for each string in `arr` and appends it to the `answer` list. If no unique substring exists, an empty string is appended to the result. The function then returns the `answer` list.",
