      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef find_possible_origins():\n    import sys\n    input = sys.stdin.read\n    data = input().split()\n    \n    N = int(data[0])\n    T_prime = data[1]\n    S = data[2:]\n    \n    def is_possible_origin(S_i, T_prime):\n        len_S = len(S_i)\n        len_T = len(T_prime)\n        \n        # Check if S_i is the same as T_prime\n        if S_i == T_prime:\n            return True\n        \n        # Check if S_i can be obtained by inserting one character into T_prime\n        if abs(len_S - len_T) == 1:\n            if len_S > len_T:\n                # S_i is longer by one character\n                for i in range(len_T + 1):\n                    if S_i[:i] + S_i[i+1:] == T_prime:\n                        return True\n            else:\n                # T_prime is longer by one character\n                for i in range(len_T):\n                    if S_i == T_prime[:i] + T_prime[i+1:]:\n                        return True\n        \n        # Check if S_i can be obtained by deleting one character from T_prime\n        if len_S == len_T:\n            for i in range(len_T):\n                if S_i == T_prime[:i] + T_prime[i+1:]:\n                    return True\n        \n        # Check if S_i can be obtained by changing one character in T_prime\n        if len_S == len_T:\n            diff_count = 0\n            for i in range(len_T):\n                if S_i[i] != T_prime[i]:\n                    diff_count += 1\n                    if diff_count > 1:\n                        return False\n            return diff_count == 1\n        \n        return False\n    \n    possible_origins = []\n    for i in range(N):\n        if is_possible_origin(S[i], T_prime):\n            possible_origins.append(i + 1)\n    \n    print(len(possible_origins))\n    if possible_origins:\n        print(' '.join(map(str, possible_origins)))\n\n# Call the function to execute with standard input\nfind_possible_origins()\n```",
