      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef find_minimum_window_width():\n    import sys\n    input = sys.stdin.read\n    data = input().split()\n    \n    n = int(data[0])\n    m = int(data[1])\n    lengths = list(map(int, data[2:]))\n    \n    # Binary search for the minimum possible width of the window\n    left, right = max(lengths), sum(lengths) + (m - 1)  # right is sum of lengths + (m-1) spaces\n    \n    def can_fit(width):\n        current_line_width = 0\n        lines_used = 1\n        \n        for length in lengths:\n            if current_line_width + length + 1 <= width:\n                current_line_width += length + 1  # include space after the word\n            else:\n                lines_used += 1\n                current_line_width = length + 1  # start a new line with this word\n                \n                if lines_used > m:\n                    return False\n        \n        return True\n    \n    # Binary search to find the minimum width\n    while left < right:\n        mid = (left + right) // 2\n        if can_fit(mid):\n            right = mid\n        else:\n            left = mid + 1\n    \n    print(left)\n\n# Call the function\nfind_minimum_window_width()\n```",
