      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef find_directed_cycle():\n    import sys\n    input = sys.stdin.read\n    data = input().split()\n    \n    N = int(data[0])\n    A = list(map(int, data[1:]))\n    \n    # Adjust the indices since they are 1-based in the problem statement\n    A = [a - 1 for a in A]\n    \n    visited = [False] * N\n    path = []\n    \n    def dfs(node):\n        if visited[node]:\n            return False\n        visited[node] = True\n        path.append(node)\n        \n        next_node = A[node]\n        if next_node in path:\n            # A cycle is detected\n            cycle_start_index = path.index(next_node)\n            cycle = path[cycle_start_index:]\n            print(len(cycle))\n            print(' '.join(str(x + 1) for x in cycle))\n            return True\n        \n        return dfs(next_node)\n    \n    # Start DFS from any node that has not been visited\n    for i in range(N):\n        if not visited[i]:\n            if dfs(i):\n                break\n\n# Call the function\nfind_directed_cycle()\n```",
