      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef largestPerimeter(nums):\n    # First, sort the array in non-increasing order\n    nums.sort(reverse=True)\n    \n    # Initialize the perimeter variable to -1, which will be returned if no valid polygon can be formed\n    perimeter = -1\n    \n    # Iterate through the sorted list to find the largest possible perimeter\n    for i in range(len(nums) - 2):\n        # Check if the sum of the three consecutive sides is greater than the largest side\n        if nums[i] < nums[i + 1] + nums[i + 2]:\n            # If the condition is satisfied, calculate the perimeter\n            perimeter = nums[i] + nums[i + 1] + nums[i + 2]\n            break  # Since the list is sorted in reverse, no need to check further\n    \n    return perimeter\n```",
