      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef find_minimal_string(a, b, c):\n    # Function to check if the given string s contains all three substrings a, b, and c\n    def contains_all(s, sub1, sub2, sub3):\n        return sub1 in s and sub2 in s and sub3 in s\n\n    # Function to find the lexicographically smallest string by comparing two strings\n    def lexicographically_smallest(s1, s2):\n        if s1 < s2:\n            return s1\n        else:\n            return s2\n\n    # Generate all possible strings that could contain a, b, and c as substrings\n    possible_strings = []\n\n    # Consider all permutations of a, b, c to generate candidate strings\n    from itertools import permutations\n    for perm in permutations([a, b, c]):\n        # Join the strings in the permutation\n        combined = ''.join(perm)\n        # Check if this combined string contains all three substrings\n        if contains_all(combined, a, b, c):\n            possible_strings.append(combined)\n\n    # Find the shortest string from the possible strings\n    min_length = float('inf')\n    min_string = \"\"\n    for string in possible_strings:\n        if len(string) < min_length:\n            min_length = len(string)\n            min_string = string\n        # If the length is the same, choose the lexicographically smallest one\n        elif len(string) == min_length:\n            min_string = lexicographically_smallest(min_string, string)\n\n    return min_string\n```",
