      "generated_answer": "Here's a Python function that fulfills the requirements:\n\n```python\ndef buy_chocolates(prices, money):\n    # Initialize variables to keep track of the minimum sum and the leftover money\n    min_sum = float('inf')\n    leftover = money\n\n    # Iterate over all pairs of chocolates to find the pair with the minimum sum\n    for i in range(len(prices)):\n        for j in range(i + 1, len(prices)):\n            # Calculate the sum of the current pair of chocolates\n            current_sum = prices[i] + prices[j]\n            \n            # If the current sum is less than the current minimum and doesn't result in debt,\n            # update the minimum sum and calculate the leftover money\n            if current_sum < min_sum and current_sum <= money:\n                min_sum = current_sum\n                leftover = money - current_sum\n\n    # Return the leftover money\n    return leftover\n```",
