      "generated_answer": "Here is the Python function that computes the maximum value of `(a XOR x) * (b XOR x)` for all `0 <= x < 2^n`, and returns the result modulo `10^9 + 7`:\n\n```python\ndef max_xor_multiplied(a, b, n):\n    MOD = 10**9 + 7\n    max_value = 0\n    \n    # Iterate over all possible x values within the range 0 to 2^n - 1\n    for x in range(1 << n):\n        # Calculate the XOR values\n        xor_a = a ^ x\n        xor_b = b ^ x\n        # Calculate the product of the XOR values\n        product = xor_a * xor_b\n        # Update the maximum value found so far\n        max_value = max(max_value, product)\n    \n    # Return the maximum value modulo 10^9 + 7\n    return max_value % MOD\n``` \n\nThis function defines a loop that iterates over all possible values of `x` within the specified range by using a bitwise left shift (`1 << n`) to calculate `2^n`. For each `x`, it computes `(a XOR x)` and `(b XOR x)`, multiplies them together, and keeps track of the maximum product found. Finally, it returns the maximum product modulo `10^9 + 7`.",
