      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\ninput = sys.stdin.read\n\ndef process_queries():\n    data = input().split()\n    n = int(data[0])\n    q = int(data[1])\n    s = list(map(int, data[2:n+2]))\n    queries = data[n+2:]\n    \n    # To keep track of flips efficiently, we use a difference array approach.\n    flip = [0] * (n + 1)\n    \n    output = []\n    query_index = 0\n    \n    for _ in range(q):\n        t = int(queries[query_index])\n        l = int(queries[query_index + 1])\n        r = int(queries[query_index + 2])\n        query_index += 3\n        \n        if t == 1:\n            # Flip the segment from l to r\n            flip[l - 1] += 1\n            if r < n:\n                flip[r] -= 1\n        else:\n            # Check if the segment from l to r is good\n            # Calculate the number of flips up to r\n            current_flips = flip[l - 1]\n            for i in range(l - 1, r):\n                if i > 0:\n                    current_flips += flip[i]\n                # Check if current character is equal to the next one\n                if s[i] == s[i + 1]:\n                    output.append(\"No\")\n                    break\n            else:\n                # If loop didn't break, the string is good\n                output.append(\"Yes\")\n    \n    # Print all results for type 2 queries\n    print(\"\\n\".join(output))\n\n# Call the function to process the queries\nprocess_queries()\n```",
