      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\ninput = sys.stdin.read\n\ndef minimize_slimes():\n    data = input().split()\n    n = int(data[0])\n    slimes = []\n    index = 1\n    for _ in range(n):\n        s = int(data[index])\n        c = int(data[index + 1])\n        slimes.append((s, c))\n        index += 2\n\n    # Dictionary to keep track of slimes by size\n    size_count = {}\n    for size, count in slimes:\n        size_count[size] = count\n\n    # Result variable to store the minimum number of slimes\n    result = 0\n\n    # Process each size in descending order\n    for size in sorted(size_count.keys(), reverse=True):\n        count = size_count[size]\n        # While we can perform syntheses\n        while count > 1:\n            # Number of syntheses we can perform\n            syntheses = count // 2\n            # Reduce the count by the number of syntheses performed\n            count -= syntheses * 2\n            # Increase the result by the number of new slimes created\n            result += syntheses\n\n    # Add the remaining slimes of each size to the result\n    for size, count in size_count.items():\n        result += count % 2\n\n    # Print the minimum number of slimes\n    print(result)\n\n# Call the function\nminimize_slimes()\n```",
