      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef find_eaten_cookie():\n    # Read dimensions of the grid\n    h, w = map(int, input().split())\n    \n    # Initialize a list to store the grid\n    grid = []\n    \n    # Read the grid from stdin\n    for _ in range(h):\n        grid.append(input())\n    \n    # Variables to store the coordinates of the top-left and bottom-right corners of the rectangle\n    top_left = None\n    bottom_right = None\n    \n    # Find the rectangle with cookies\n    for i in range(h):\n        for j in range(w):\n            if grid[i][j] == '#':\n                if top_left is None:\n                    top_left = (i, j)\n            else:\n                if top_left is not None and bottom_right is None:\n                    bottom_right = (i - 1, j)\n                    break\n        if bottom_right is not None:\n            break\n    \n    # Adjust the bottom-right corner to the actual last cookie position\n    for i in range(bottom_right[0], -1, -1):\n        if grid[i][bottom_right[1]] == '#':\n            bottom_right = (i, bottom_right[1])\n            break\n    \n    # Find the eaten cookie by checking which cookie is missing in the rectangle\n    for i in range(top_left[0], bottom_right[0] + 1):\n        for j in range(top_left[1], bottom_right[1] + 1):\n            if grid[i][j] == '.':\n                print(i + 1, j + 1)\n                return\n\n# Call the function to execute\nfind_eaten_cookie()\n```",
