      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\ninput = sys.stdin.read\n\ndef max_operations():\n    data = input().split()\n    index = 0\n    N = int(data[index])\n    index += 1\n    M = int(data[index])\n    index += 1\n    \n    # Initialize adjacency list and weights\n    adjacency_list = [[] for _ in range(N)]\n    weights = [0] * N\n    pieces = [0] * N\n    \n    # Read edges\n    for _ in range(M):\n        u = int(data[index]) - 1\n        index += 1\n        v = int(data[index]) - 1\n        index += 1\n        adjacency_list[u].append(v)\n        adjacency_list[v].append(u)\n    \n    # Read weights and pieces\n    for i in range(N):\n        weights[i] = int(data[index])\n        index += 1\n    for i in range(N):\n        pieces[i] = int(data[index])\n        index += 1\n    \n    # Total pieces initially\n    total_pieces = sum(pieces)\n    \n    # Calculate the sum of weights for each vertex\n    weight_sums = [0] * N\n    for i in range(N):\n        weight_sums[i] = weights[i] * pieces[i]\n    \n    # Initialize the number of operations\n    operations = 0\n    \n    # Repeat until all pieces are distributed\n    while total_pieces > 0:\n        # Find the vertex with the maximum weight sum\n        max_weight_sum = max(weight_sums)\n        max_index = weight_sums.index(max_weight_sum)\n        \n        # Calculate the number of pieces that can be moved from this vertex\n        pieces_to_move = min(pieces[max_index], total_pieces)\n        \n        # Perform the operation\n        total_pieces -= pieces_to_move\n        operations += pieces_to_move\n        \n        # Update the weight sums\n        weight_sums[max_index] -= max_weight_sum\n        \n        # Distribute pieces to adjacent vertices\n        for neighbor in adjacency_list[max_index]:\n            if weights[neighbor] < weights[max_index]:\n                # Calculate the number of pieces to place on the neighbor\n                pieces_to_place = min(pieces_to_move, total_pieces // (weights[max_index] - weights[neighbor]))\n                pieces[neighbor] += pieces_to_place\n                weight_sums[neighbor] += (weights[neighbor] - weights[max_index]) * pieces_to_place\n                total_pieces -= pieces_to_place\n    \n    print(operations)\n\n# Call the function to execute\nmax_operations()\n```",
