      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef is_strictly_superior(N, M, products):\n    for i in range(N):\n        for j in range(N):\n            if i != j:\n                # Check if product i is at least as expensive as product j\n                if products[i][0] >= products[j][0]:\n                    # Convert list of functions to a set for easier comparison\n                    functions_i = set(products[i][1])\n                    functions_j = set(products[j][1])\n                    # Check if all functions of product i are in product j\n                    if functions_i.issubset(functions_j):\n                        # Check if product i is strictly more expensive or has additional functions\n                        if products[i][0] > products[j][0] or not functions_j.issubset(functions_i):\n                            print(\"Yes\")\n                            return\n    print(\"No\")\n\n# Reading input\nimport sys\ninput = sys.stdin.read\ndata = input().splitlines()\n\nN, M = map(int, data[0].split())\nproducts = []\n\nfor i in range(1, N + 1):\n    line = data[i].split()\n    price = int(line[0])\n    num_functions = int(line[1])\n    functions = list(map(int, line[2:2 + num_functions]))\n    products.append((price, functions))\n\n# Call the function\nis_strictly_superior(N, M, products)\n```",
