      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\nfrom heapq import heappop, heappush\nfrom collections import defaultdict\n\ndef max_candies_visited(H, W, T, grid):\n    # Directions for moving in the grid: right, left, down, up\n    directions = [(0, 1), (0, -1), (1, 0), (-1, 0)]\n    \n    # Locate the start and goal positions\n    start = goal = None\n    for i in range(H):\n        for j in range(W):\n            if grid[i][j] == 'S':\n                start = (i, j)\n            elif grid[i][j] == 'G':\n                goal = (i, j)\n    \n    # Priority queue for BFS with (distance, candies, x, y)\n    pq = []\n    heappush(pq, (0, 0, start[0], start[1]))\n    \n    # Visited dictionary to store the maximum candies collected at each position with distance\n    visited = defaultdict(lambda: -float('inf'))\n    visited[(start[0], start[1])] = 0\n    \n    # BFS with priority queue\n    while pq:\n        dist, candies, x, y = heappop(pq)\n        \n        # If we reach the goal and within allowed moves\n        if (x, y) == goal:\n            if dist <= T:\n                print(candies)\n                return\n        \n        # Explore neighbors\n        for dx, dy in directions:\n            nx, ny = x + dx, y + dy\n            if 0 <= nx < H and 0 <= ny < W and grid[nx][ny] != '#':\n                n_dist = dist + 1\n                n_candies = candies + (1 if grid[nx][ny] == 'o' else 0)\n                if n_dist <= T:\n                    if visited[(nx, ny)] < n_candies:\n                        visited[(nx, ny)] = n_candies\n                        heappush(pq, (n_dist, n_candies, nx, ny))\n    \n    # If goal is not reachable within allowed moves\n    print(-1)\n\n# Read input\ninput = sys.stdin.read\ndata = input().split()\nH, W, T = map(int, data[:3])\ngrid = [data[i + 3][:W] for i in range(H)]\n\n# Call the function\nmax_candies_visited(H, W, T, grid)\n```",
