    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef are_horizontally_adjacent():\n    # Read integers A and B from standard input\n    A, B = map(int, input().split())\n\n    # Determine the board positions of A and B\n    # The board is structured as:\n    # 1 2 3\n    # 4 5 6\n    # 7 8 9\n    # We calculate the position by subtracting 1 from the number and finding the quotient and remainder\n    position_A = (A - 1) // 3\n    position_B = (B - 1) // 3\n\n    # Check if A and B are in the same row (i.e., have the same quotient)\n    if position_A == position_B:\n        # Calculate the column positions\n        column_A = (A - 1) % 3\n        column_B = (B - 1) % 3\n\n        # Check if the columns are adjacent\n        if abs(column_A - column_B) == 1:\n            print('Yes')\n            return\n\n    # If not adjacent horizontally, print 'No'\n    print('No')\n\n# Call the function\nare_horizontally_adjacent()\n```",
