      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef min_sum_k_avoiding_array(n, k):\n    # Initialize the array that will hold the minimum sum\n    min_sum = 0\n    # Start adding numbers from 1 to n to the sum\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        # Check if adding i and (i+k) exceeds n, which would mean a pair sums to k\n        # and avoid adding i+k to the sum\n        if i + k <= n:\n            min_sum += i + (i + k)\n        else:\n            min_sum += i\n    # Since every number from i+k is added only once, we need to subtract k from the sum\n    # because we added one extra k for each i from 1 to n-k\n    min_sum -= k * (n - k)\n    return min_sum\n```",
