    "prediction": "glm-4-air",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\nfrom collections import deque\n\ndef find_minimum_f():\n    input = sys.stdin.read\n    data = input().split()\n    \n    index = 0\n    n = int(data[index])\n    index += 1\n    \n    edges = []\n    for _ in range(n - 1):\n        a = int(data[index])\n        b = int(data[index + 1])\n        edges.append((a, b))\n        index += 2\n    \n    cs = list(map(int, data[index:index + n]))\n    \n    # Create adjacency list for the tree\n    adjacency_list = [[] for _ in range(n + 1)]\n    for a, b in edges:\n        adjacency_list[a].append(b)\n        adjacency_list[b].append(a)\n    \n    # Helper function to calculate the sum of C values and distances\n    def calculate_f(start):\n        queue = deque([(start, 0)])  # (current_node, current_distance)\n        visited = [False] * (n + 1)\n        visited[start] = True\n        sum_f = 0\n        node_count = [0] * (n + 1)\n        node_count[start] = 1\n        \n        while queue:\n            current, dist = queue.popleft()\n            sum_f += cs[current - 1] * dist\n            for neighbor in adjacency_list[current]:\n                if not visited[neighbor]:\n                    visited[neighbor] = True\n                    queue.append((neighbor, dist + 1))\n                    node_count[neighbor] = 1\n                # If already visited, add the count of nodes in the subtree of the current node\n                else:\n                    node_count[neighbor] += node_count[current]\n        \n        return sum_f, node_count\n    \n    # Calculate f for the first node and get the initial node counts\n    f_sum, node_counts = calculate_f(1)\n    \n    # Use the subtree sizes to adjust the sum for all nodes\n    min_f = f_sum\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        # Subtract the contribution of the subtree rooted at i\n        # and add the contribution of the tree outside the subtree rooted at i\n        subtree_contribution = cs[i - 1] * node_counts[i]\n        outside_contribution = (sum(cs) - subtree_contribution) * node_counts[i]\n        adjusted_f = f_sum - subtree_contribution + outside_contribution\n        min_f = min(min_f, adjusted_f)\n    \n    print(min_f)\n\n# Call the function to execute\nfind_minimum_f()\n```",
