      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef process_cards():\n    import sys\n    input = sys.stdin.read\n    data = input().split()\n    \n    N = int(data[0])\n    cards = []\n    \n    index = 1\n    for i in range(N):\n        A = int(data[index])\n        C = int(data[index + 1])\n        cards.append((A, C, i + 1))\n        index += 2\n    \n    # Sort cards by strength (A) in ascending order, and by cost (C) in descending order\n    cards.sort(key=lambda x: (x[0], -x[1]))\n    \n    # Initialize the stack to keep track of cards that cannot be discarded\n    stack = []\n    \n    # Iterate over sorted cards\n    for A, C, idx in cards:\n        # Maintain the condition that no card can be discarded\n        while stack and stack[-1][0] < A and stack[-1][1] > C:\n            stack.pop()\n        stack.append((A, C, idx))\n    \n    # Output the result\n    print(len(stack))\n    print(' '.join(str(card[2]) for card in stack))\n\n# Call the function to execute\nprocess_cards()\n```",
