      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef find_minimum_travel_time():\n    import sys\n    input = sys.stdin.read\n    data = input().split()\n    \n    # Read the first line of input for N, A, B, C\n    index = 0\n    N = int(data[index])\n    A = int(data[index + 1])\n    B = int(data[index + 2])\n    C = int(data[index + 3])\n    index += 4\n    \n    # Read the distance matrix\n    D = []\n    for i in range(N):\n        D.append(list(map(int, data[index:index + N])))\n        index += N\n    \n    # Initialize the cost matrix with infinity\n    cost = [[float('inf')] * N for _ in range(N)]\n    \n    # Set the diagonal to 0 as the distance from a city to itself is 0\n    for i in range(N):\n        cost[i][i] = 0\n    \n    # Fill the cost matrix with minimum travel times considering both car and train\n    for i in range(N):\n        for j in range(N):\n            if i != j:\n                cost[i][j] = min(D[i][j] * A, D[i][j] * B + C)\n    \n    # Apply the Floyd-Warshall algorithm to find the shortest path from city 1 to city N\n    for k in range(N):\n        for i in range(N):\n            for j in range(N):\n                if cost[i][j] > cost[i][k] + cost[k][j]:\n                    cost[i][j] = cost[i][k] + cost[k][j]\n    \n    # Output the minimum time from city 1 to city N\n    print(cost[0][N - 1])\n\n# Call the function to execute\nfind_minimum_travel_time()\n```",
