    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef is_intersection():\n    N = int(sys.stdin.readline().strip())\n    chords = [tuple(map(int, sys.stdin.readline().split())) for _ in range(N)]\n\n    # This function determines if two chords (a1, b1) and (a2, b2) intersect\n    def intersect(a1, b1, a2, b2):\n        # Normalize the points such that a1 < b1 and a2 < b2\n        if a1 > b1:\n            a1, b1 = b1, a1\n        if a2 > b2:\n            a2, b2 = b2, a2\n        \n        # Check if the intervals intersect\n        return a1 < b2 and b1 > a2\n\n    # Sort the chords by their first endpoint\n    chords.sort()\n\n    # Check for intersections using the sorted order\n    for i in range(N - 1):\n        for j in range(i + 1, N):\n            a1, b1 = chords[i]\n            a2, b2 = chords[j]\n            if intersect(a1, b1, a2, b2):\n                print('Yes')\n                return\n\n    print('No')\n\n# Call the function\nis_intersection()\n```",
