    "prediction": "glm-4-air",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef can_form_string():\n    import sys\n    input = sys.stdin.read\n    data = input().split()\n    \n    N = int(data[0])\n    M = int(data[1])\n    S = data[2]\n    T = data[3]\n    \n    # Create a list of tuples (character, count) for S\n    s_grouped = []\n    count = 1\n    for i in range(1, N):\n        if S[i] == S[i - 1]:\n            count += 1\n        else:\n            s_grouped.append((S[i - 1], count))\n            count = 1\n    s_grouped.append((S[-1], count))  # Append the last group\n    \n    # Create a list of tuples (character, count) for T\n    t_grouped = []\n    count = 1\n    for i in range(1, M):\n        if T[i] == T[i - 1]:\n            count += 1\n        else:\n            t_grouped.append((T[i - 1], count))\n            count = 1\n    t_grouped.append((T[-1], count))  # Append the last group\n    \n    # Check if T can be used to form S\n    if len(t_grouped) > len(s_grouped):\n        print(\"No\")\n        return\n    \n    # Reverse both lists to start comparison from the end\n    s_grouped.reverse()\n    t_grouped.reverse()\n    \n    # Check if each group in T can match a group in S\n    for t_char, t_count in t_grouped:\n        if not s_grouped:\n            print(\"No\")\n            return\n        s_char, s_count = s_grouped.pop()\n        if t_char != s_char or t_count > s_count:\n            print(\"No\")\n            return\n    \n    # If all groups match correctly\n    print(\"Yes\")\n\n# Call the function\ncan_form_string()\n```",
