      "generated_answer": "Here's the Python function that calculates the maximum length of all alternating subarrays in a given list of integers, `nums`:\n\n```python\ndef max_alternating_subarray_length(nums):\n    max_length = -1\n    current_length = 1\n\n    for i in range(1, len(nums)):\n        # Check if the current pair is alternating\n        if (nums[i] - nums[i-1]) * (1 if i % 2 == 1 else -1) == 1:\n            current_length += 1\n            max_length = max(max_length, current_length)\n        else:\n            # If not alternating, reset the current length to 1\n            current_length = 1\n    \n    # If max_length remains -1, it means no alternating subarray was found\n    return max_length if max_length > 1 else -1\n```\n\nThis function iterates over the array, checking if each consecutive pair of elements is alternating according to the given rule. If it is, it increments the current length of the alternating subarray. If it's not, it resets the current length to 1. The function keeps track of the maximum length found and returns it. If no alternating subarray of length greater than 1 is found, it returns -1.",
