      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef find_min_operations_to_form_consecutive_o():\n    import sys\n    input = sys.stdin.read\n    data = input().split()\n    \n    H = int(data[0])\n    W = int(data[1])\n    K = int(data[2])\n    S = data[3:H+3]\n    \n    # Initialize the minimum operations to a large number\n    min_operations = float('inf')\n    \n    # Check horizontally\n    for i in range(H):\n        current_count = 0\n        max_count = 0\n        needed_changes = 0\n        for j in range(W):\n            if S[i][j] == 'o':\n                current_count += 1\n            else:\n                if current_count >= K:\n                    max_count = max(max_count, current_count)\n                current_count = 0\n                needed_changes = 0\n        \n        if current_count >= K:\n            max_count = max(max_count, current_count)\n        \n        if max_count >= K:\n            min_operations = min(min_operations, K - max_count)\n    \n    # Check vertically\n    for j in range(W):\n        current_count = 0\n        max_count = 0\n        needed_changes = 0\n        for i in range(H):\n            if S[i][j] == 'o':\n                current_count += 1\n            else:\n                if current_count >= K:\n                    max_count = max(max_count, current_count)\n                current_count = 0\n                needed_changes = 0\n        \n        if current_count >= K:\n            max_count = max(max_count, current_count)\n        \n        if max_count >= K:\n            min_operations = min(min_operations, K - max_count)\n    \n    # If min_operations was updated, return it, otherwise return -1\n    return min_operations if min_operations != float('inf') else -1\n\n# Call the function and print the result\nprint(find_min_operations_to_form_consecutive_o())\n```",
