      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef minimum_score_for_final_grade():\n    import sys\n    input = sys.stdin.read\n    data = input().split()\n    \n    N = int(data[0])\n    X = int(data[1])\n    scores = list(map(int, data[2:]))\n    \n    # Sort the scores to easily find the minimum and maximum\n    scores.sort()\n    \n    # Calculate the current sum of scores excluding the highest and lowest\n    current_sum = sum(scores[1:N-1])\n    \n    # Calculate the minimum score needed in the last round to reach or exceed the final grade X\n    required_score = X - current_sum\n    \n    # Check if the required score is possible\n    if required_score > 100:\n        print(-1)\n    else:\n        # Check if the required score is greater than the maximum possible score\n        # or if it is less than the minimum possible score (0 in this case)\n        if required_score > scores[-2]:\n            print(-1)\n        else:\n            # Find the smallest score that is >= required_score and less than the second highest score\n            for score in scores[:N-2]:\n                if score >= required_score:\n                    print(required_score)\n                    return\n            # If no such score is found, it means the required score is between the second highest and the highest\n            print(required_score)\n\n# Call the function\nminimum_score_for_final_grade()\n```",
