      "generated_answer": "Here's the Python function body that solves the problem described:\n\n```python\ndef find_beautiful_indices(s, a, b, k):\n    def find_substring_indices(text, substring):\n        return [i for i in range(len(text) - len(substring) + 1) if text[i:i + len(substring)] == substring]\n\n    a_indices = find_substring_indices(s, a)\n    b_indices = find_substring_indices(s, b)\n    beautiful_indices = []\n\n    for i in a_indices:\n        for j in b_indices:\n            if abs(j - i) <= k:\n                beautiful_indices.append(i)\n                break\n\n    return sorted(list(set(beautiful_indices)))  # Remove duplicates and sort before returning\n\n# Note: The function `find_substring_indices` is a helper function that finds all starting indices\n# of the substring in the given text.\n```\n\nThis function defines a helper function `find_substring_indices` to find all occurrences of a substring within a string, and then iterates through the indices of `a` to check if there exists a corresponding index of `b` such that the absolute difference is less than or equal to `k`. The resulting indices are collected in a list, duplicates are removed, and the list is sorted before being returned.",
