      "generated_answer": "Here's the Python function that matches the description provided:\n\n```python\ndef count_pattern_subarrays(nums, pattern):\n    n = len(nums)\n    m = len(pattern)\n    count = 0\n\n    for i in range(n - m):\n        match = True\n        for j in range(m):\n            if pattern[j] == 1 and nums[i + j + 1] <= nums[i + j]:\n                match = False\n                break\n            elif pattern[j] == 0 and nums[i + j + 1] != nums[i + j]:\n                match = False\n                break\n            elif pattern[j] == -1 and nums[i + j + 1] >= nums[i + j]:\n                match = False\n                break\n        if match:\n            count += 1\n    return count\n``` \n\nThis function iterates through all possible subarrays of length `m + 1` in `nums` and checks each subarray against the `pattern` criteria. If a subarray matches the pattern, the `count` is incremented. The final count of matching subarrays is returned at the end of the function.",
