      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\ninput = sys.stdin.read\n\ndef max_currency_units():\n    data = input().split()\n    N = int(data[0])\n    A = list(map(int, data[1:N+1]))\n    pairs = []\n    index = N + 1\n    for i in range(N - 1):\n        S = int(data[index])\n        T = int(data[index + 1])\n        pairs.append((S, T))\n        index += 2\n\n    # Initialize the maximum currency units of the last country\n    max_units = A[-1]\n\n    # Traverse from the second last to the first country\n    for i in range(N - 2, -1, -1):\n        S, T = pairs[i]\n        # Calculate the maximum possible units of currency for country i\n        # It's either keep the current amount or perform the operation optimally\n        # to maximize the currency of the next country\n        max_units = max(max_units, A[i] - (S - 1) * T + max_units)\n\n    # Output the maximum units of the last country\n    print(max_units)\n\n# Call the function\nmax_currency_units()\n```",
