      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef find_most_expensive_set_meal():\n    import sys\n    input = sys.stdin.read\n    data = input().split()\n    \n    # Read N, M, L from the first line\n    index = 0\n    N = int(data[index])\n    M = int(data[index + 1])\n    L = int(data[index + 2])\n    index += 3\n    \n    # Read the costs of main dishes\n    a = list(map(int, data[index:index + N]))\n    index += N\n    \n    # Read the costs of side dishes\n    b = list(map(int, data[index:index + M]))\n    index += M\n    \n    # Read the pairs (c_i, d_i) that cannot be combined\n    forbidden_pairs = set()\n    for _ in range(L):\n        c = int(data[index]) - 1\n        d = int(data[index + 1]) - 1\n        forbidden_pairs.add((c, d))\n        index += 2\n    \n    # Initialize the maximum price to be the sum of the most expensive main and side dishes\n    max_price = max(a) + max(b)\n    \n    # Iterate over all possible combinations of main and side dishes\n    for i in range(N):\n        for j in range(M):\n            if (i, j) not in forbidden_pairs:\n                current_price = a[i] + b[j]\n                if current_price > max_price:\n                    max_price = current_price\n    \n    # Print the most expensive valid set meal price\n    print(max_price)\n\n# Call the function to execute it\nfind_most_expensive_set_meal()\n```",
