      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\ninput = sys.stdin.read\n\ndef count_intersections():\n    data = input().split()\n    N = int(data[0])\n    intervals = []\n    \n    index = 1\n    for _ in range(N):\n        l, r = int(data[index]), int(data[index + 1])\n        intervals.append((l, r))\n        index += 2\n\n    # Using a line sweep algorithm\n    events = []\n    for l, r in intervals:\n        events.append((l, 'start'))\n        events.append((r, 'end'))\n\n    # Sort events: first by coordinate, then by type ('end' before 'start' for the same coordinate)\n    events.sort(key=lambda x: (x[0], x[1] == 'start'))\n\n    active_intervals = 0\n    intersection_count = 0\n    last_end = -1\n\n    for coordinate, typ in events:\n        if typ == 'start':\n            if active_intervals > 0 and coordinate > last_end:\n                intersection_count += active_intervals\n            active_intervals += 1\n        else:\n            active_intervals -= 1\n            last_end = coordinate\n\n    print(intersection_count)\n\n# Call the function\ncount_intersections()\n```",
