      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef fireworks_days():\n    import sys\n    input = sys.stdin.read\n    data = input().split()\n    \n    N = int(data[0])\n    M = int(data[1])\n    A = list(map(int, data[2:]))\n    \n    # Initialize the result list with large values\n    result = [float('inf')] * N\n    \n    # Set the days with fireworks to 0 days later\n    for day in A:\n        result[day - 1] = 0\n    \n    # Calculate the minimum days until the next fireworks for each day\n    min_days = float('inf')\n    for i in range(N - 1, -1, -1):\n        min_days = min(min_days, result[i])\n        result[i] = min_days\n    \n    # Print the results\n    for days in result:\n        print(days)\n\n# Call the function\nfireworks_days()\n```",
