      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef find_minimum_time_to_play_stage_n():\n    import sys\n    input = sys.stdin.read\n    data = input().split()\n    \n    N = int(data[0])\n    stages = []\n    index = 1\n    for i in range(N - 1):\n        A = int(data[index])\n        B = int(data[index + 1])\n        X = int(data[index + 2])\n        stages.append((A, B, X))\n        index += 3\n    \n    # Initialize the minimum time to reach each stage with infinity\n    min_time = [float('inf')] * (N + 1)\n    min_time[1] = 0  # It takes 0 seconds to start at stage 1\n    \n    # Process each stage\n    for i in range(1, N):\n        A, B, X = stages[i - 1]\n        \n        # If we can reach stage i, update the time to reach stage i+1 and X\n        if min_time[i] != float('inf'):\n            min_time[i + 1] = min(min_time[i + 1], min_time[i] + A)\n            if X <= N:\n                min_time[X] = min(min_time[X], min_time[i] + B)\n    \n    # The answer is the minimum time to reach stage N\n    print(min_time[N])\n\n# Call the function to execute\nfind_minimum_time_to_play_stage_n()\n```",
