      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef count_transformations(s, t, k):\n    MOD = 10**9 + 7\n    n = len(s)\n    \n    # Check if s and t can be transformed into each other\n    if sorted(s) != sorted(t):\n        return 0\n    \n    # Calculate the number of ways to transform s into t in exactly k operations\n    def count_ways(s, t, k):\n        # If k is 0 or 1, check if s is already equal to t or can be transformed in one operation\n        if k == 0:\n            return 1 if s == t else 0\n        elif k == 1:\n            return 1 if s in [t[i:] + t[:i] for i in range(n)] else 0\n        \n        # Initialize ways to 0\n        ways = 0\n        \n        # Check each possible suffix to rotate\n        for i in range(1, n):\n            # If the rotated string equals t, increment ways\n            if s[i:] + s[:i] == t:\n                # If k is even, consider the ways to achieve this in k operations\n                if k % 2 == 0:\n                    ways += count_ways(s[i:] + s[:i], t, k // 2 - 1)\n                    ways %= MOD\n        \n        return ways\n    \n    # Start the recursive count\n    return count_ways(s, t, k)\n```",
