ts is 4 + 3 = 7.\n\n \nConstraints:\n\nn == nums.length\nm == queries.length\n1 <= m <= n <= 10^5\n1 <= nums[i] <= 10^5\nqueries[i].length == 2\n0 <= index_i, k_i <= n - 1",
    "prediction": "glm-4-air",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef process_queries(nums, queries):\n    n = len(nums)\n    marked = [False] * n\n    unmarked_nums = []\n    answer = []\n\n    for num in nums:\n        if not marked[nums.index(num)]:\n            unmarked_nums.append(num)\n\n    for index, k in queries:\n        # Mark the element at the given index if it's not already marked\n        if not marked[index]:\n            marked[index] = True\n            # Update the list of unmarked numbers if the current number was unmarked\n            if nums[index] in unmarked_nums:\n                unmarked_nums.remove(nums[index])\n        \n        # If there are enough unmarked elements, mark k smallest ones\n        if k <= len(unmarked_nums):\n            for _ in range(k):\n                smallest_unmarked = unmarked_nums.pop(0)\n                marked[smallest_unmarked] = True\n        else:\n            # If not enough unmarked elements, mark all of them\n            while unmarked_nums:\n                smallest_unmarked = unmarked_nums.pop(0)\n                marked[smallest_unmarked] = True\n\n        # Calculate the sum of the remaining unmarked elements\n        answer.append(sum(unmarked_nums))\n\n    return answer\n```",
