    "prediction": "glm-4-air",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef minimum_mountain_triplet_sum(nums):\n    n = len(nums)\n    if n < 3:\n        return -1\n    \n    # Initialize minimum sum to infinity\n    min_sum = float('inf')\n    \n    # Iterate through each possible 'j' (the peak of the mountain)\n    for j in range(1, n-1):\n        left_max_index = -1\n        right_min_index = -1\n        \n        # Find the left max index for the current 'j'\n        for i in range(j-1, -1, -1):\n            if nums[i] < nums[j]:\n                left_max_index = i\n            else:\n                break\n        \n        # Find the right min index for the current 'j'\n        for k in range(j+1, n):\n            if nums[k] < nums[j]:\n                right_min_index = k\n            else:\n                break\n        \n        # Check if a valid mountain triplet is found\n        if left_max_index != -1 and right_min_index != -1:\n            # Calculate the sum of the mountain triplet\n            current_sum = nums[left_max_index] + nums[j] + nums[right_min_index]\n            # Update the minimum sum found\n            min_sum = min(min_sum, current_sum)\n    \n    # If no mountain triplet was found, return -1, otherwise return the minimum sum\n    return -1 if min_sum == float('inf') else min_sum\n```",
