er is 2.\n\nSample Input 2\n\n1 2\r\n2\r\n1 2\n\nSample Output 2\n\n0\r\n\nS_1 already contains both 1 and M, so the minimum number of operations required is 0.\n\nSample Input 3\n\n3 5\r\n2\r\n1 3\r\n2\r\n2 4\r\n3\r\n2 4 5\n\nSample Output 3\n\n-1\n\nSample Input 4\n\n4 8\r\n3\r\n1 3 5\r\n2\r\n1 2\r\n3\r\n2 4 7\r\n4\r\n4 6 7 8\n\nSample Output 4\n\n2",
