      "generated_answer": "```python\nfrom collections import deque\nimport sys\ninput = sys.stdin.read\n\ndef min_operations_to_combine():\n    data = input().split()\n    index = 0\n    n = int(data[index])\n    m = int(data[index + 1])\n    index += 2\n\n    # Initialize distance and visited arrays\n    dist = [-1] * (m + 1)\n    visited = [False] * (m + 1)\n\n    # Process each set\n    for _ in range(n):\n        a = int(data[index])\n        index += 1\n        elements = list(map(int, data[index:index + a]))\n        index += a\n\n        # Initialize BFS if set contains 1 and update distances\n        if 1 in elements:\n            for num in elements:\n                if not visited[num]:\n                    visited[num] = True\n                    dist[num] = 0\n\n    # BFS to find the minimum distance to M\n    queue = deque()\n    for i in range(1, m + 1):\n        if visited[i]:\n            queue.append(i)\n\n    while queue:\n        current = queue.popleft()\n        if current == m:\n            print(dist[current])\n            return\n\n        # Explore neighbors\n        for neighbor in [current - 1, current + 1]:\n            if 1 <= neighbor <= m and not visited[neighbor]:\n                visited[neighbor] = True\n                dist[neighbor] = dist[current] + 1\n                queue.append(neighbor)\n\n    # If M is not reachable\n    print(-1)\n\n# Call the function\nmin_operations_to_combine()\n```",
