      "generated_answer": "Here is a Python function that implements the described behavior:\n\n```python\ndef min_operations_to_equal(s1, s2, s3):\n    # Base case: if any string is empty, they cannot be made equal\n    if not s1 or not s2 or not s3:\n        return -1\n\n    # If all strings are equal, no operation is needed\n    if s1 == s2 == s3:\n        return 0\n\n    # Recursive function to determine the minimum operations\n    def recursive_min(s1, s2, s3):\n        # If any of the strings has a length of 1, they cannot be made equal\n        if len(s1) == 1 or len(s2) == 1 or len(s3) == 1:\n            return -1\n        \n        # Check if the last characters are the same\n        if s1[-1] == s2[-1] == s3[-1]:\n            # If so, reduce the problem by removing the last character of each string\n            return recursive_min(s1[:-1], s2[:-1], s3[:-1])\n        else:\n            # If not, consider all possibilities of removing the last character from one of the strings\n            min_ops = float('inf')\n            if len(s1) > 1:\n                min_ops = min(min_ops, recursive_min(s1[:-1], s2, s3))\n            if len(s2) > 1:\n                min_ops = min(min_ops, recursive_min(s1, s2[:-1], s3))\n            if len(s3) > 1:\n                min_ops = min(min_ops, recursive_min(s1, s2, s3[:-1]))\n            \n            return min_ops if min_ops != float('inf') else -1\n\n    # Start the recursive process and add 1 because we are always reducing the strings\n    result = recursive_min(s1, s2, s3)\n    return result if result != -1 else -1\n``` \n\nThis function first checks if the strings are already equal or if any of them are empty, in which case it returns the appropriate value. Then it defines a recursive function `recursive_min` that reduces the problem size by removing the last character of each string when the last characters are the same, or by trying different combinations of strings to remove the last character from when they are not the same. The main function then calls this recursive function and returns the result.",
