    "prediction": "glm-4-air",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The period of a cosine function is given by \\( \\frac{2\\pi}{|\\omega|} \\), where \\( \\omega \\) is the angular frequency. For the signal \\( x_1(t) \\), we have two cosine functions with angular frequencies \\( 3\\pi \\) and \\( 5\\pi \\). The periods of these components are \\( \\frac{2\\pi}{3\\pi} = \\frac{2}{3} \\) and \\( \\frac{2\\pi}{5\\pi} = \\frac{2}{5} \\). The overall period of the signal is the least common multiple (LCM) of these two periods, which is \\( \\frac{2}{3} \\times 3 = 2 \\). \n\nThus, the correct answer is \\boxed{H}.",
