    "global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9474",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Consider a 26-key typewriter. Suppose that pushing a key results in printing that letter or the next (with equal probability). Thus A results in A or B, ..., Z results in Z or A. What is the capacity of this channel in bits?\n\nOptions: \nA. 2.0\nB. 2.5\nC. 4.7\nD. 4.5\nE. 1.8\nF. 4.1\nG. 5.0\nH. 3.0\nI. 6.0\nJ. 3.7\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "glm-4-air",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}\n\nThe capacity of a channel can be calculated using the Shannon-Hartley theorem, which states that channel capacity is the maximum rate at which information can be transmitted over a communication channel. With each key press having two equally likely outcomes, the entropy per key is \\( \\log_2(2) = 1 \\) bit. However, since there is a 50% chance that the next key will be the next letter in the sequence, this adds an additional 0.5 bits of information (as the next letter has 2 options out of 27 total possibilities, which is approximately \\( \\log_2(\\frac{2}{27}) \\) bits). Thus, the total capacity is about \\( 1 + 0.5 = 1.5 \\) bits per key press, but since each key can also result in its own letter with equal probability, the total capacity doubles to 2 bits per key press. Therefore, the correct answer is B (2.0 bits).",
