    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}\n\nThe correct answer is B. To determine a single integer from 256 possibilities, you need to ask enough questions to reduce the possibilities down to one. Since every question halves the remaining possibilities, it takes $\\log_2(256) = 8$ questions to determine the exact integer. However, since the question asks for deterministic questions that are equivalent to the halving process, and considering that each question could potentially eliminate half of the remaining numbers, you would need 64 such deterministic questions, because each question eliminates one of the 2^8 (256) subsets that correspond to the 256 numbers. This is equivalent to a binary search over the subsets.",
