    "global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_2116",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In class, John's teacher tells him that she will give him the coin and bill for each picture he can correctly identify on the face of the penny, nickel, dime, quarter, half-dollar, dollar bill, and five-dollar bill. John cannot identify any of them although he has been handling money for 17 years. His inability to remember the pictures most likely results from\n\nOptions: \nA. sensory memory decay\nB. retroactive interference\nC. failure to encode\nD. failure to reconstruct\nE. false memory formation\nF. lack of attention\nG. failure to retrieve\nH. confabulation\nI. deep processing\nJ. proactive interference\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "glm-4-air",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}\n\nJohn's inability to remember the pictures on the money he has been handling is most likely due to a failure to encode. Since he has been handling money for 17 years but cannot recall the images, it suggests that he never processed the information deeply enough to commit it to memory. Sensory memory decay (A) would involve forgetting immediately after perception, which does not fit the scenario of handling money over a long period. Retroactive interference (B) and proactive interference (J) involve interference from other learned information, which is not indicated in the context provided. Failure to reconstruct (D) and failure to retrieve (G) imply that the information was encoded at some point but cannot be accessed now, which is not supported by the scenario. Lack of attention (F) could be a contributing factor but is not a form of memory failure. False memory formation (E) and confabulation (H) involve remembering events or information inaccurately, which is not the case here. Deep processing (I) is the opposite of what is happening, as deep processing would lead to better memory retention.",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 197,
        "output_tokens": 226,
        "total_tokens": 423
      },
      "provider": "zhipu",
