      "generated_answer": "To find the exchange rate of pesos to dollars for 2007, we divide the total dollars spent by the total pesos spent. For 2007, the company spent $736.0 million on 8.1 billion Mexican pesos. Therefore, the exchange rate is calculated as:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Exchange Rate} = \\frac{\\$736.0 \\text{ million}}{8.1 \\text{ billion MXN}} = \\frac{736,000,000 \\text{ USD}}{8,100,000,000 \\text{ MXN}}\n\\]\n\nSimplifying the division gives us:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Exchange Rate} = \\frac{736}{8100} \\approx 0.0909 \\text{ USD per MXN}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{0.0909}\n\\]",
