      "generated_answer": "To find the percentage increase in berth capacity for the European cruise market between 2012 and 2016, we need to compare the additional berths expected to be added to the total number of berths at the beginning of the period.\n\nThe number of additional berths expected to be added is 28,000.\n\nThe number of berths at the end of 2011 was 155,000.\n\nThe percentage increase is calculated by dividing the additional berths by the initial number of berths and then multiplying by 100 to get the percentage.\n\n\\[\n\\text{Percentage Increase} = \\left( \\frac{\\text{Additional Berths}}{\\text{Initial Berths}} \\right) \\times 100 = \\left( \\frac{28000}{155000} \\right) \\times 100 \\approx 18.06\\%\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{18.06}\n\\]",
