    "global index": "MMLUPro_business_378",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: (a) Convert 678 cm to feet. (b) Convert 316 liters to dry pints. (c) Convert 50 kg to pounds.\n\nOptions: \nA. 21 ft, 625 pints, 105 pounds\nB. 22 ft, 575.12 pints, 110 pounds\nC. 19 ft, 650 pints, 140 pounds\nD. 22 ft, 668 pints, 150 pounds\nE. 24 ft, 600 pints, 120 pounds\nF. 23 ft, 560 pints, 125 pounds\nG. 20 ft, 613 pints, 111 pounds\nH. 25 ft, 580 pints, 115 pounds\nI. 20 ft, 550 pints, 100 pounds\nJ. 18 ft, 590 pints, 130 pounds\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "glm-4-air",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}\n\nTo convert centimeters to feet, you divide by 30.48 (since 1 foot = 30.48 cm). So, 678 cm / 30.48 cm/ft = approximately 22.15 feet, which rounds to 22 feet. For liters to dry pints, since 1 liter is approximately 2.11338 dry pints, 316 liters * 2.11338 pints/liter = approximately 665.47 pints, but since dry pints are used for volumes of dry goods, this conversion is unusual and not standard. However, if we were converting to US liquid pints, which is more common, it would be closer to 665.28 pints. Lastly, to convert kilograms to pounds, you multiply by 2.20462 (since 1 kg = 2.20462 lbs). Thus, 50 kg * 2.20462 lbs/kg = approximately 110.23 pounds. The closest answers to these conversions, even considering the unusual dry pint conversion, are given in option B.",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 256,
        "output_tokens": 230,
        "total_tokens": 486
      },
      "provider": "zhipu",
