  },
  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_business_530",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: You have just redesigned your kitchen. The new floor dimensions are 7'6\" × 11'8\". Now you want to cover the floor with linoleum, which sells for $1.79 per running foot in 6' width, what is the best way to cover the floor? How much will it cost?\n\nOptions: \nA. $48.60\nB. $26.85\nC. $30.99\nD. $42.56\nE. $29.99\nF. $38.40\nG. $31.50\nH. $23.94\nI. $20.12\nJ. $35.70\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "glm-4-air",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}\n\nTo cover the floor with linoleum, you first need to calculate the area of the floor in square feet. The dimensions are 7.5 feet by 11.6667 feet, resulting in an area of approximately 87.5 square feet. Since the linoleum is sold in a 6-foot width, you would need to purchase 11.6667 feet of linoleum (which is the longer dimension) to cover the width. To find the linear feet needed, you'd calculate 87.5 square feet divided by 6 feet, which equals approximately 14.5833 linear feet. At $1.79 per running foot, the total cost would be about $26.11 for the material. However, none of the options match this exact price, indicating that there might be an error in the provided options or rounding may have occurred. Upon reviewing the provided options and rounding to the nearest cent, option D ($42.56) seems to be the closest to a reasonable estimate considering the cost of linoleum and the area of the floor, but this discrepancy suggests a potential issue with the provided answers. If the options were calculated based on the dimensions and price given, the correct answer should have been closer to $26.11.",
