    "global index": "MMLUPro_business_52",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The average salary of the Bedford Manufacturing Co. rose 60% during a 10-year period. This rise amounted to $42.50 a week. (a) Find the average weekly salary at the beginning of the 10-year period, and (b) at the end of the 10-year period.\n\nOptions: \nA. $75.83, $118.33\nB. $90.83, $133.33\nC. $80.83, $123.33\nD. $55.83, $98.33\nE. $50.83, $93.33\nF. $70.83, $113.33\nG. $45.83, $88.33\nH. $85.83, $128.33\nI. $60.83, $103.33\nJ. $65.83, $108.33\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "glm-4-air",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}\n\nTo solve for the average weekly salary at the beginning of the period, we use the formula for the final salary after a percentage increase: Final Salary = Initial Salary * (1 + percentage increase). Given that the increase is 60%, we have that Final Salary = Initial Salary * 1.60. We know the increase is $42.50, so we set up the equation $42.50 = Initial Salary * 0.60. Solving for Initial Salary gives us $42.50 / 0.60 = $70.83. However, this doesn't match any of the options directly, so there seems to be a mistake in the provided options. Recalculating correctly, we find that the initial salary was $70.83 / 0.60 ≈ $117.73, which still does not match the options given. Given the options and the context, it seems there might be an error in the question or options provided. Nevertheless, based on the closest reasonable estimate to the calculated $117.73 (which is not one of the choices), option B ($90.83, $133.33) appears to be the closest to the correct answer assuming an approximation, but it is not mathematically exact.",
