    "global index": "MMLUPro_business_379",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Firestone's Clothing Store had an August 1 inventory of $2,300. During August, new merchandise purchases totaled $1,125,and sales were $3,485. If the margin on sales was 18%, estimate the final inventory on August 31.\n\nOptions: \nA. $800.00\nB. $567.30\nC. $1,500.00\nD. $627.30\nE. $940.00\nF. $2,000.00\nG. $1,938.00\nH. $2,857.70\nI. $1,725.00\nJ. $3,485\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "glm-4-air",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{D}. To estimate the final inventory, first calculate the cost of goods sold (COGS) by multiplying the sales by the complement of the margin (100% - 18% = 82%). COGS is $3,485 * 82% = $2,847.7. Then subtract COGS from the sum of the beginning inventory and new purchases ($2,300 + $1,125 = $3,425), which gives the ending inventory: $3,425 - $2,847.7 = $627.3. \n\nTherefore, the estimated final inventory on August 31 is $627.30.",
