    "global index": "MMLUPro_business_247",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Suppose we are given the following information. Use this information to calculate abnormal return. Rf: 4%\nRm: 12%\nBeta of the Portfolio: 1.8\nBeginning Value of Portfolio: $50,000\nEnding Value of Portfolio: $60,000\nWhat is the abnormal return?\n\nOptions: \nA. 0.025\nB. 0.035\nC. 0.016\nD. 0.012\nE. 0.030\nF. 0.040\nG. 0.008\nH. 0.010\nI. 0.020\nJ. 0.050\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "glm-4-air",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To calculate the abnormal return, we must first find the expected return of the portfolio using the Capital Asset Pricing Model (CAPM), which is given by the formula: Expected Return = Rf + Beta * (Rm - Rf). Plugging in the values, we get: Expected Return = 4% + 1.8 * (12% - 4%) = 4% + 1.8 * 8% = 4% + 14.4% = 18.4%. \n\nNext, we calculate the actual return of the portfolio: Actual Return = (Ending Value - Beginning Value) / Beginning Value = ($60,000 - $50,000) / $50,000 = $10,000 / $50,000 = 0.20 or 20%.\n\nFinally, the abnormal return is the actual return minus the expected return: Abnormal Return = 20% - 18.4% = 1.6% or 0.016.\n\nThe correct letter choice is \\boxed{C}.",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 206,
        "output_tokens": 217,
