    "global index": "MMLUPro_business_413",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Loretta Gould has been offered a position as salesperson for the Houston Oil Company. Her manager estimates that her sales will amount to approximately $80,000 the first year. She may accept one of two pay schedules: (1) a salary of $8,000 plus commission of 1% of sales or (2) a salary of $5,800 plus a commission of 5% of sales over $30,000. Which pay schedule is better? By how much is it better?\n\nOptions: \nA. Both schedules are the same\nB. Schedule (1) is better by $300\nC. Both schedules are better by different amounts depending on sales\nD. Schedule (1) is better by $1,200\nE. Schedule (2) is better by $1,200\nF. Schedule (2) is better by $700\nG. Schedule (1) is better by $700\nH. Schedule (1) is better by $500\nI. Schedule (2) is better by $500\nJ. Schedule (2) is better by $300\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "glm-4-air",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}\n\nSchedule (2) is better by $1,200. Calculating Loretta's earnings under Schedule (1), she would earn $8,000 salary plus 1% of $80,000 in sales, which equals $800 in commission, totaling $8,800. Under Schedule (2), her salary is $5,800 and she gets 5% commission on sales over $30,000, which is 5% of $50,000 (since $80,000 - $30,000 = $50,000), or $2,500 in commission. Adding this to her salary gives her $8,300, which is $1,200 more than Schedule (1).",
