    "global index": "MMLUPro_business_573",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: JamesTaggertwishes to paint the walls of his storage room. The room's dimensions are 14' by 10' by 8(1/2)' . One quart of paint costing $9.80 will cover 36 sq. ft. Labor costs is $5 per quart or fractionthere of. Find his cost for painting the room.\n\nOptions: \nA. $210.70\nB. $143.20\nC. $158.40\nD. $177.60\nE. $220.50\nF. $185.90\nG. $192.80\nH. $199.50\nI. $165.30\nJ. $205.00\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "glm-4-air",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}\n\nTo find the cost for painting the room, we first calculate the total area of the walls to be painted: the room has two pairs of opposite walls, so the total area is \\(2 \\times (14' \\times 8.5') + 2 \\times (10' \\times 8.5') = 238 + 170 = 408 \\text{ sq. ft.}\\). Since one quart covers 36 sq. ft., we need \\(\\frac{408}{36} \\approx 11.33\\) quarts of paint. At $5 per quart of labor, the total labor cost is \\(11.33 \\times $5 = $56.65\\). The cost for 11.33 quarts of paint at $9.80 per quart is \\(11.33 \\times $9.80 = $111.55\\). Adding the paint and labor costs gives us $111.55 + $56.65 = $168.20. The closest option to this total cost is B. $143.20, but since none of the options match our calculated cost, it seems there might be an error in the provided options. However, based on the closest calculation, the intended correct answer is B. $143.20.",
