    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The acid-test ratio (also known as the quick ratio) is calculated by subtracting inventory from current assets and then dividing by current liabilities. However, since the context does not provide any inventory, we can calculate it directly using the provided current assets and liabilities. The acid-test ratio is therefore calculated as (Cash + Marketable Securities + Accounts Receivable) / (Notes Payable + Accounts Payable) = ($7,300 + $14,200 + $2,120) / ($1,400 + $1,850) = $23,620 / $3,250 = approximately 7.27. \n\n\\boxed{G}",
