    "prediction": "glm-4-air",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}\n\nThe correct answer is C. When the deficit is negative, it means the government has a budget surplus, which can reduce the debt if the surplus is used to pay it down. The federal debt is the accumulation of past deficits, not future ones (thus A and F are incorrect), and a positive deficit increases the debt, not decreases it (thus B, H, and I are incorrect). The debt cannot be negative, and the deficit is not the accumulation of future debts, nor are the deficit and debt always equal (thus D, E, G, and J are incorrect).",
