    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "\\boxed{G}\n\nThe characteristic roots of a moving average (MA) process are found by solving the characteristic equation associated with the recursion of the MA process. For the given MA process $y_t = -3u_{{t-1}} + u_{{t-2}} + u_t$, the characteristic equation is $1 + 3z^{-1} - z^{-2} = 0$. Solving this equation for $z$ gives us the characteristic roots. Simplifying and solving the equation results in the roots 1 and -3.",
