    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "\\boxed{G}\n\nThe expression $\\hat{{u}}^t \\hat{{u}} represents the transpose of vector $\\hat{{u}}$ multiplied by vector $\\hat{{u}}$. Assuming $\\hat{{u}}$ is a k x 1 column vector, its transpose $\\hat{{u}}^t$ is a 1 x k row vector. Multiplying a 1 x k row vector by a k x 1 column vector results in a 1 x 1 scalar, but since the question is asking for dimensions, the operation itself does not change the dimensions. The dimensions of $\\hat{{u}}^t \\hat{{u}} would be k x k because you are essentially calculating the dot product of each component of the vector with itself, which is a square matrix.",
