      "generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}\n\nThe consistency, unbiasedness, and efficiency (best linear unbiased estimator, BLUE) of the OLS estimator require the following assumptions: $E(u_t) = 0$ (zero mean of the error term), $\\text{Var}(u_t) = \\sigma^2$ (homoscedasticity), and $\\text{Cov}(u_t, u_{t-j}) = 0$ for all $j \\neq 0$ (no serial correlation). The normality assumption $u_t \\sim N(0, \\sigma^2)$ is not required for these properties, although it is necessary for hypothesis testing involving t and F distributions.",
