      "generated_answer": "\\boxed{E}\n\nEGARCH (Exponential GARCH) models overcome the limitations of standard GARCH models by allowing for asymmetric effects of positive and negative shocks on volatility (ii), addressing the issue of non-negativity of the estimated coefficients (i), and not being constrained to symmetric responses of volatility to shocks (iii). However, GARCH models, including EGARCH, do allow for a feedback from volatility to returns, so (iv) is not a correct criticism of GARCH models.",
