  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_economics_5594",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following statements are true concerning information criteria?\n\n(i) Adjusted R-squared is an information criterion\n\n(ii) If the residual sum of squares falls when an additional term is added, the value of the information criterion will fall\n\n(iii) Akaike's information criterion always leads to model orders that are at least as large as those of Schwarz's information criterion\n\n(iv) Akaike's information criterion is consistent\n\nOptions: \nA. (ii) and (iv) only\nB. (ii) and (iii) only\nC. (i), (ii), (iii), and (iv)\nD. (i) and (iv) only\nE. (i) and (iii) only\nF. (i), (iii), and (iv) only\nG. (i) and (ii) only\nH. (ii), (iii), and (iv) only\nI. (iii) and (iv) only\nJ. (i), (ii), and (iii) only\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "glm-4-air",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}\n\nAdjusted R-squared is not an information criterion; it's a measure of the proportion of variance explained by the model that is adjusted for the number of predictors. The information criteria (like AIC and BIC) take into account both the goodness of fit and the model complexity. While adding an additional term generally decreases the residual sum of squares, it does not necessarily lead to a better information criterion value because the penalty for adding more parameters could outweigh the improvement in fit. Akaike's information criterion (AIC) does not always lead to model orders as large as those of Schwarz's information criterion (BIC), as BIC includes a larger penalty for the number of parameters. Akaike's information criterion is consistent, meaning it selects the true model with probability tending to one as the sample size tends to infinity.",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 273,
        "output_tokens": 173,
        "total_tokens": 446
