      "generated_answer": "\\boxed{G}\n\nThe 'Lotus principle' is derived from the Permanent Court of International Justice's decision in the S.S. Lotus case (1927). It is best reflected by the idea that \"restrictions upon the independence of States cannot therefore be presumed,\" meaning that unless an action is prohibited by international law, it is permissible. This principle emphasizes the sovereignty and freedom of states in the international arena.",
