      "generated_answer": "\\boxed{H}\n\nUnder the common law of riparian rights, each landowner whose property touches the stream has equal rights to reasonable use of the water. However, domestic use is typically given priority over agricultural use. Therefore, the judgment should be for the rancher because his domestic use is superior to the millionaire's agricultural use.",
