      "generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}\n\nThe plaintiff will prevail because the company's policy is discriminatory and violates her civil rights. The Equal Protection Clause of the Fourteenth Amendment prohibits gender-based discrimination by states, and the policy of excluding women as a group is a clear violation of this principle. The fact that the company is a lessee of county land and operates with the county's approval and a state-issued license implies state action, making it subject to constitutional protections.",
