      "generated_answer": "To find the three-digit positive integer $\\underline{a}\\,\\underline{b}\\,\\underline{c}$, we first note that the base nine representation $\\underline{b}\\,\\underline{c}\\,\\underline{a}_{\\text{nine}}$ translates to $9b + c + a \\times 9^2$. Since this must equal the base ten number $\\underline{a}\\,\\underline{b}\\,\\underline{c}$, we have $100a + 10b + c = 9b + c + 81a$. Simplifying this equation gives $19a = 8b$. The smallest positive integer solution occurs when $a = 4$ and $b = 9$ (since $19 \\times 4 = 76$ and $8 \\times 9 = 72$), which means $c$ can be any digit from 0 to 9. Therefore, the three-digit number is $\\boxed{49c}$.",
