  {
    "global index": "AIME_16",
    "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Find the remainder when\\[\\binom{{\\binom{{3}}{{2}}{{2}} + \\binom{{\\binom{{4}}{{2}}{{2}} + \\dots +  \\binom{{\\binom{{40}}{{2}}{{2}}\\]is divided by $1000$.\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "glm-4-air",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To solve this problem, we need to recognize the pattern and apply properties of binomial coefficients. The expression inside the binomial coefficient simplifies as follows:\n\n\\[\\binom{3}{2} = 3\\]\n\\[\\binom{4}{2} = 6\\]\n\\[\\vdots\\]\n\\[\\binom{40}{2} = \\frac{40 \\times 39}{2} = 780\\]\n\nThe sum inside the outer binomial coefficient is the arithmetic series of these terms. The sum of an arithmetic series is given by \\( \\frac{n}{2} \\times (\\text{first term} + \\text{last term}) \\), where \\( n \\) is the number of terms.\n\nThe number of terms is \\( 40 - 3 + 1 = 38 \\), and the sum of the series is \\( \\frac{38}{2} \\times (3 + 780) = 19 \\times 783 \\).\n\nNow we need to find \\( \\binom{19 \\times 783}{2} \\) modulo 1000. Since the binomial coefficient is only affected by the last three digits of the numerator, we can compute \\( \\binom{19 \\times 783}{2} \\) modulo 1000 by considering only the last three digits of \\( 19 \\times 783 \\).\n\n\\( 19 \\times 783 \\) modulo 1000 is the same as \\( 19 \\times 783 \\) modulo 1000, because \\( 19 \\times 783 = 14877 \\), and the last three digits of 14877 are 877. Therefore, we need to calculate \\( \\binom{877}{2} \\) modulo 1000.\n\n\\[\\binom{877}{2} = \\frac{877 \\times 876}{2} = 383632\\]\n\nTaking this modulo 1000 gives:\n\n\\[383632 \\mod 1000 = 632\\]\n\nThus, the remainder when the original expression is divided by 1000 is \\boxed{632}.",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 132,
        "output_tokens": 453,
        "total_tokens": 585
      },
      "provider": "zhipu",
      "error": null
