  {
    "global index": "AsDiv_1425",
    "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: A boat goes 30 km upstream and 44 km downstream in 10 hours. In 13 hours, it can go 40 km upstream and 55 km downstream.\n\nQuestion: Determine the speed of the stream and that of boat in still water.\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "glm-4-air",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Let the speed of the boat in still water be \\( b \\) km/h and the speed of the stream be \\( s \\) km/h. Upstream, the boat's speed is \\( b - s \\), and downstream, it is \\( b + s \\). Using the given information, we can set up the following equations based on distance equals rate times time:\n\nFor the first scenario: \\((b - s) \\cdot t_1 + (b + s) \\cdot t_2 = 30 + 44\\) where \\(t_1\\) and \\(t_2\\) are the times taken to travel upstream and downstream, respectively.\n\nFor the second scenario: \\((b - s) \\cdot t_3 + (b + s) \\cdot t_4 = 40 + 55\\) where \\(t_3\\) and \\(t_4\\) are the times taken to travel upstream and downstream, respectively.\n\nSince the total time for the first scenario is 10 hours and for the second scenario is 13 hours, we can write:\n\n\\(t_1 + t_2 = 10\\) and \\(t_3 + t_4 = 13\\).\n\nAlso, we know that \\(t_1 = \\frac{30}{b - s}\\) and \\(t_2 = \\frac{44}{b + s}\\), and \\(t_3 = \\frac{40}{b - s}\\) and \\(t_4 = \\frac{55}{b + s}\\). Substituting these into the time equations gives us:\n\n\\(\\frac{30}{b - s} + \\frac{44}{b + s} = 10\\) and \\(\\frac{40}{b - s} + \\frac{55}{b + s} = 13\\).\n\nBy solving these two equations simultaneously, we get:\n\nSpeed of the stream \\(s = 3\\) km/h and speed of the boat in still water \\(b = 13\\) km/h.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{{s = 3 \\text{ km/h}, b = 13 \\text{ km/h}}}\n\\]",
