    "global index": "AsDiv_1432",
    "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: A railway half ticket costs half the full fare and the reservation charge is the same on half ticket as on full ticket. One reserved first class from Michigan to Massachusetts costs $216 and one full and one half reserved first class tickets cost $327.\n\nQuestion: What is the basic first class full fare and what is the reservation charge?\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "glm-4-air",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Let the basic first class fare be \\( x \\) dollars and the reservation charge be \\( y \\) dollars. From the given information, we have the following two equations:\n\n1. \\( x + y = 216 \\) (since one reserved first class ticket costs $216)\n2. \\( x + \\frac{1}{2}x + 2y = 327 \\) (since one full and one half reserved first class tickets cost $327)\n\nSimplifying the second equation, we get:\n\n\\( \\frac{3}{2}x + 2y = 327 \\)\n\nNow, we have a system of linear equations:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\nx + y &= 216 \\\\\n\\frac{3}{2}x + 2y &= 327\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\nMultiplying the first equation by 2 to eliminate \\( y \\), we get:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n2x + 2y &= 432 \\\\\n\\frac{3}{2}x + 2y &= 327\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\nSubtracting the second equation from the first, we find:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{2}x = 105 \\Rightarrow x = 210\n\\]\n\nSubstituting \\( x = 210 \\) into the first equation, we find:\n\n\\[\n210 + y = 216 \\Rightarrow y = 6\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the basic first class full fare is \\( \\boxed{210} \\) dollars and the reservation charge is \\( \\boxed{6} \\) dollars.",
