    "global index": "MATH_99",
    "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem and provide the final answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: If $\\mathbf{{a}} = \\begin{{pmatrix}} 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\end{{pmatrix}},$ then find the vector $\\mathbf{{v}}$ such that $\\mathbf{{a}} \\cdot \\mathbf{{v}} = 2$ and $\\mathbf{{a}} \\times \\mathbf{{v}} = \\begin{{pmatrix}} 1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\end{{pmatrix}}.$\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "glm-4-air",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Let $\\mathbf{v} = \\begin{pmatrix} x \\\\ y \\\\ z \\end{pmatrix}$. From the given conditions, we have the system:\n\\[\n\\begin{cases}\n1 \\cdot x + 1 \\cdot y + 1 \\cdot z = 2, \\\\\n\\begin{vmatrix} 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & y & z \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1 \\end{vmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}.\n\\end{cases}\n\\]\nThis gives us:\n\\[\n\\begin{cases}\nx + y + z = 2, \\\\\ny - z = 1.\n\\end{cases}\n\\]\nSolving this system, we find $x = 2 - y - z$, and substituting into the second equation gives $y - z = 1$. Let $z = t$, then $y = t + 1$ and $x = 1 - t$. Thus, $\\mathbf{v} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 - t \\\\ t + 1 \\\\ t \\end{pmatrix}$, where $t$ is any real number.\n\n\\boxed{$\\mathbf{v} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 - t \\\\ t + 1 \\\\ t \\end{pmatrix}$ for any real number $t$.}",
