      "generated_answer": "To find $z_{2002}$, we first need to calculate the first few terms of the sequence to see if there is a pattern or if the sequence is periodic. Starting with $z_0 = \\frac{1}{137} + i$, we can compute $z_1 = F(z_0) = \\frac{\\frac{1}{137} + i + i}{\\frac{1}{137} + i - i} = \\frac{\\frac{1}{137} + 2i}{\\frac{1}{137}} = 1 + 2i$. Then, $z_2 = F(z_1) = \\frac{1 + 2i + i}{1 + 2i - i} = \\frac{1 + 3i}{1 + i}$. Continuing this process, we find that $z_3 = F(z_2) = -i$. Noting that $F(-i) = i$, we see that the sequence repeats every two terms. Therefore, $z_{2002} = z_{2 \\cdot 1001} = z_2 = 1 + 3i$. \n\n\\boxed{1 + 3i}",
