      "generated_answer": "The probability that Alice wins on her first flip is \\( \\frac{1}{2} \\). If she doesn't win on her first flip, the game returns to the same state it was at the beginning, with Alice now having another chance to win. The probability of Alice eventually winning is the sum of the probability of her winning immediately (which is \\( \\frac{1}{2} \\)) and the probability that she doesn't win on the first flip, then wins on her subsequent turn (which is \\( \\frac{1}{2} \\times \\frac{1}{2} \\times \\text{the probability that Alice eventually wins} \\)). Let \\( p \\) be the probability that Alice wins. Then, \\( p = \\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{1}{2} \\times \\frac{1}{2} \\times p \\), so \\( p = \\frac{2}{3} \\).\n\n\\boxed{\\(\\frac{2}{3}\\)}",
