    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "\\[\\frac{{(2^4 + \\frac{1}{4})(4^4 + \\frac{1}{4}) \\dotsm [(2n)^4 + \\frac{1}{4}]}}{{(1^4 + \\frac{1}{4})(3^4 + \\frac{1}{4}) \\dotsm [(2n - 1)^4 + \\frac{1}{4}]}} = \\frac{{(2^4 + \\frac{1}{4})(4^4 + \\frac{1}{4}) \\dotsm [(2n)^4 + \\frac{1}{4}]}}{{(1 + \\frac{1}{4})(3 + \\frac{1}{4}) \\dotsm [(2n - 1) + \\frac{1}{4}]}} \\cdot \\frac{{(1 + \\frac{1}{4})(3 + \\frac{1}{4}) \\dotsm [(2n - 1) + \\frac{1}{4}]}}{{(1^4 + \\frac{1}{4})(3^4 + \\frac{1}{4}) \\dotsm [(2n - 1)^4 + \\frac{1}{4}]}}.\\]\n\nThe second fraction simplifies to 1 because each term in the numerator and the denominator cancel out. The first fraction simplifies to:\n\\[\\frac{{(2^4 + \\frac{1}{4})(4^4 + \\frac{1}{4}) \\dotsm [(2n)^4 + \\frac{1}{4}]}}{{(2^4 + \\frac{1}{4})(4^4 + \\frac{1}{4}) \\dotsm [(2n)^4 + \\frac{1}{4}]}} \\cdot \\frac{{1 + \\frac{1}{4}}}{{1 + \\frac{1}{4}}} \\cdot \\frac{{3 + \\frac{1}{4}}}{{3 + \\frac{1}{4}}} \\dotsm \\frac{{(2n - 1) + \\frac{1}{4}}}{{(2n - 1) + \\frac{1}{4}}}.\\]\n\nThis simplifies to \\(\\frac{{2n + \\frac{1}{4}}}{{1 + \\frac{1}{4}}} = 2n\\).\n\n\\boxed{2n}",
