      "generated_answer": "To find the integers \\( n \\) such that \\( f(n) = n \\), first set \\( y = 0 \\) in the functional equation to get \\( f(x) + f(0) = f(x) - x^2 - 1 \\), which simplifies to \\( f(0) = -x^2 - 1 \\). Plugging \\( x = 0 \\) into this gives \\( f(0) = -1 \\). Next, set \\( y = 1 \\) in the original equation to get \\( f(x) + f(1) = f(x + 1) - x - 1 \\). Since \\( f(1) = 1 \\), we have \\( f(x) + 1 = f(x + 1) - x - 1 \\), which rearranges to \\( f(x + 1) = f(x) + x \\). By induction, \\( f(n) = f(1) + (n - 1) \\), so \\( f(n) = 1 + (n - 1) = n \\). Therefore, \\( f(n) = n \\) for all integers \\( n \\).\n\n\\boxed{\\(\\mathbb{Z}\\)}",
