      "generated_answer": "\\boxed{J}\n\nThe probability of drawing a face card (Jack, Queen, or King) on the first draw is 12/52 (since there are 12 face cards in a deck of 52 cards). After drawing a face card, there are now 51 cards left in the deck, and the probability of drawing an ace on the second draw is 4/51 (since there are 4 aces remaining). The combined probability is (12/52) * (4/51) which simplifies to 4/221.",
