      "generated_answer": "The best interpretation of a 95 percent confidence interval for the mean income per family is:\n\n\\boxed{D}\n\nThis is because a 95 percent confidence interval means that we are 95% confident that the true mean income per family of all students in the school lies between $35,095 and $45,005. Options A, E, and J incorrectly interpret the interval as applying to the individual incomes or family incomes rather than the mean. Options B and C misunderstand the nature of confidence intervals. Option F refers to the median instead of the mean, and option H incorrectly asserts certainty. Option G is incorrect because it refers to the sample mean, but the interval is meant to estimate the population mean.",
