      "generated_answer": "To find $g(25)$, we need to determine what value of $x$ makes $f(x) = 25$. Setting $3x^2 - 2 = 25$ gives us $3x^2 = 27$, so $x^2 = 9$. This means $x$ could be $3$ or $-3$. Plugging $x = 3$ into $g(f(x)) = x^2 + x + 1$ gives us $g(25) = 3^2 + 3 + 1 = 13$. Plugging $x = -3$ into the same equation gives us $g(25) = (-3)^2 - 3 + 1 = 7$. However, since we are looking for the sum of all possible values of $g(25)$, we add $13$ and $7$ to get $20$. Thus, the correct answer is \\boxed{I}.",
